From: openRuyi contributors
Subject: [PATCH] Use a constant format string with analysis.Pass.Reportf

Go 1.27 vet rejects non-constant format strings passed to Reportf. Keep the
existing diagnostic text while passing it as a string argument.

--- a/analyzer.go
+++ b/analyzer.go
@@ -225,1 +225,1 @@
-		pass.Reportf(gd.Pos(), fmtWrongOrderMsg(gd.Tok.String(), l))
+		pass.Reportf(gd.Pos(), "%s", fmtWrongOrderMsg(gd.Tok.String(), l))
@@ -246,1 +246,1 @@
-			pass.Reportf(fd.Pos(), fmtWrongOrderMsg(token.FUNC.String(), l))
+			pass.Reportf(fd.Pos(), "%s", fmtWrongOrderMsg(token.FUNC.String(), l))
